  "style": {
    "name": "Mughal sun-temple — Lapis Meridian",
    "rationale": "Second pass: replaced the flat gold pediment with a true bulbous onion dome whose belly (w17, x20-36) overhangs its quartz drum (w13, x22-34) so it never reads as a pyramid; both corner minarets are bonded into the body (x4-7 / x49-52) and project as engaged relief, none detached; the central iwan is now a 6-deep pointed-arch pocket (back wall z=-6) with a gold ogee field and crimson medallion; every former flat field is broken with quartz pilaster strips, three gold string-courses, 2-deep gold-backed niches with crimson quatrefoil rosettes, and a chattri kiosk flanking each side of the dome; held the lapis-dominant split-complementary palette (lapis field, quartz+gold trim, crimson accent) against the white marble reference rather than copying its color."
  },
